# Frontend Template - Cursor Rules

## Tech Stack

- React 19
- Vite 7
- TypeScript 5 (strict mode)
- TanStack Query (React Query)
- React Router DOM 7
- React Hook Form + Zod
- Axios
- Tailwind CSS 4
- ESLint 9 + Prettier
- Untitled UI React

## Project Structure

```
src/
├── components/
│   ├── application/     # Application-level components (DataTable, ErrorBoundary, etc.)
│   ├── base/            # Base UI components
│   │   └── _rhf/        # React Hook Form adapted components
│   ├── guards/          # Route guards
│   └── page-loading.tsx
├── contexts/            # React contexts
├── hooks/               # Custom hooks
├── layouts/             # Layout components
├── libs/               # Utilities and helpers
│   ├── storage/        # Token storage
│   ├── validators/     # Zod validation schemas
│   └── env.ts          # Environment configuration
├── modules/            # Feature modules (feature-based architecture)
│   ├── auth/
│   ├── users/
│   └── common/         # Shared utilities
├── pages/              # Page components
├── providers/          # App providers
├── routes/             # Route configuration
├── services/           # Axios instances
├── styles/             # Global CSS
└── utils/              # Utility functions
```

## Naming Conventions

| Type                 | Convention                  | Example                                 |
| -------------------- | --------------------------- | --------------------------------------- |
| Page components      | PascalCase + Page           | `UsersPage.tsx`                         |
| Module UI components | PascalCase                  | `UsersTable.tsx`, `CreateUserModal.tsx` |
| Module type files    | PascalCase                  | `User.ts`, `CreateUserRequest.ts`       |
| Other files          | kebab-case                  | `use-user-profile.ts`, `auth-api.ts`    |
| Component exports    | PascalCase                  | `UserProfile`                           |
| Hooks                | camelCase with `use` prefix | `useUserProfile`, `useUsers.ts`         |
| Types                | PascalCase                  | `User`, `CreateUserRequest`             |
| Validators           | camelCase                   | `signinValidator`                       |
| API files            | camelCase + API             | `usersAPI.ts`                           |
| Constants files      | kebab-case                  | `query-keys.ts`                         |

## Import Order (Enforced by ESLint)

Imports MUST follow this exact order:

```typescript
// 1. React and external libraries
import { useState } from 'react';
import { useQuery } from '@tanstack/react-query';
import { z } from 'zod';

// 2. Internal modules (@/modules/*)
import { useUsers } from '@/modules/users';
import { Role } from '@/modules/auth';

// 3. Components (@/components/*)
import { DataTable } from '@/components/application/data-table/data-table';
import { Button } from '@/components/base/buttons/button';

// 4. Other internal imports (@/*)
import { usePageMetadata } from '@/libs/usePageMetadata';
import { cx } from '@/utils/cx';

// 5. Relative imports (../ and ./)
import { usePostsFilters } from '../libs';
import type { Post } from '../types';
```

## Type Conventions

- Use `type` for object shapes and unions:

  ```typescript
  type User = { id: string; name: string };
  type Status = 'active' | 'inactive';
  ```

- Use `interface` for component props (enables declaration merging):

  ```typescript
  interface ButtonProps {
    children: ReactNode;
    onClick?: () => void;
  }
  ```

- Request/Response types use PascalCase with suffix:

  ```typescript
  type CreateUserRequest = { ... };
  type UpdateUserRequest = { ... };
  type UsersResponse = PaginatedResponse<User>;
  ```

- Filter types extend `BaseTableFilters`:
  ```typescript
  interface UsersFilters extends BaseTableFilters {
    search: string;
    role: Role | '';
  }
  ```

## Module Structure

Each module follows this layered architecture:

```
modules/[module-name]/
├── api/
│   └── [module]API.ts        # API endpoint functions
├── constants/
│   ├── query-keys.ts         # Query key factory
│   └── index.ts              # Constants exports
├── libs/
│   ├── use[Module]Filters.ts # Table filter hooks
│   └── index.ts              # Libs exports
├── services/
│   └── use[Action].ts        # TanStack Query hooks
├── types/
│   ├── [TypeName].ts         # Individual type files (PascalCase)
│   └── index.ts              # Types exports
├── ui/
│   ├── [Module]Table.tsx     # Table component
│   ├── [Module]Filters.tsx   # Filters component
│   ├── Create[Entity]Modal.tsx
│   ├── Edit[Entity]Modal.tsx
│   ├── Delete[Entity]Dialog.tsx
│   └── index.ts              # UI exports
└── index.ts                  # Public module exports
```

## Decision Rules

### When to use Module Generator (`pnpm generate:module`)

- Creating a new CRUD resource with list/create/edit/delete
- Standard REST API endpoints
- Needs table, filters, and modals

### When to create manually

- Non-CRUD features (auth, settings, dashboards)
- Custom UI patterns
- Complex business logic

### When to use factories

- `createCrudAPI` → Standard REST endpoints (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE)
- `createQueryKeys` → Any module with React Query
- `useTableFilters` → Any paginated list with URL-synced filters

### When to add to common module

- Utility is used by 2+ modules
- Generic enough to be reusable
- Not tied to specific business logic

## Component Patterns

### Page Component Structure

```typescript
export const EntityPage = () => {
  // 1. Page metadata (ALWAYS include)
  usePageMetadata({ title: "Entities" });

  // 2. State for modals
  const [isCreateOpen, setIsCreateOpen] = useState(false);
  const [editing, setEditing] = useState<Entity | null>(null);
  const [deleting, setDeleting] = useState<Entity | null>(null);

  // 3. Render
  return (
    <PageWrapper>
      <PageHeader>...</PageHeader>
      <PageContent>
        <QueryErrorBoundary>
          <EntityTable onEdit={setEditing} onDelete={setDeleting} />
        </QueryErrorBoundary>
        <CreateEntityModal isOpen={isCreateOpen} onClose={() => setIsCreateOpen(false)} />
        <EditEntityModal user={editing} isOpen={!!editing} onClose={() => setEditing(null)} />
        <DeleteEntityDialog user={deleting} isOpen={!!deleting} onClose={() => setDeleting(null)} />
      </PageContent>
    </PageWrapper>
  );
};
```

### Table Component Structure

```typescript
export const EntityTable = ({ onEdit, onDelete }: Props) => {
  // 1. Filters hook
  const { filters, setPage, setSearch, hasActiveFilters } = useEntityFilters();

  // 2. Data fetching
  const { data, isLoading } = useEntities(filters);

  // 3. Column definitions (memoized if needed)
  const columns = useMemo(() => [...], [onEdit, onDelete]);

  // 4. Render DataTable
  return <DataTable ... />;
};
```

### Modal Component Structure

```typescript
export const CreateEntityModal = ({ isOpen, onClose }: Props) => {
  // 1. Mutation hook
  const { mutate, isPending } = useCreateEntity();

  // 2. Form setup
  const { control, handleSubmit, reset } = useForm({
    resolver: zodResolver(schema),
    defaultValues: { ... }
  });

  // 3. Submit handler
  const onSubmit = (data: FormData) => {
    mutate(data, {
      onSuccess: () => {
        reset();
        onClose();
      },
    });
  };

  // 4. Render modal with form
  return (
    <DialogTrigger isOpen={isOpen} onOpenChange={(open) => !open && onClose()}>
      <ModalOverlay isDismissable>
        <Modal className="max-w-md">
          <Dialog>
            <form onSubmit={handleSubmit(onSubmit)}>...</form>
          </Dialog>
        </Modal>
      </ModalOverlay>
    </DialogTrigger>
  );
};
```

## API & Data Fetching Patterns

### Query Keys

- ALWAYS use query key factories from `constants/query-keys.ts`
- NEVER define query keys inline
- Use `createQueryKeys` factory from `@/modules/common` when possible

```typescript
// ✅ Correct
import { userQueryKeys } from '../constants';
useQuery({ queryKey: userQueryKeys.list(params) });

// ❌ Wrong
useQuery({ queryKey: ['users', 'list'] });
```

### API Layer

- NEVER use axios directly in components
- ALWAYS use module API layer
- Use `createCrudAPI` factory for standard REST endpoints

```typescript
// ✅ Correct
import { usersAPI } from '../api/usersAPI';
const data = await usersAPI.getUsers();

// ❌ Wrong
const data = await axiosInstance.get('/users');
```

### Service Hooks

- ALWAYS use service hooks (React Query) for data fetching
- NEVER mix API calls with UI logic

```typescript
// ✅ Correct
const { data, isLoading } = useUsers(filters);

// ❌ Wrong
const Component = () => {
  const response = await axiosInstance.get('/users');
};
```

### Error Handling

- ALWAYS use `getErrorMessage` from `@/modules/common` for consistent error messages
- NEVER use generic error messages

```typescript
// ✅ Correct
import { getErrorMessage } from '@/modules/common';
onError: (error: unknown) => {
  toast.error(getErrorMessage(error, 'Failed to create user'));
};

// ❌ Wrong
onError: () => {
  toast.error('Failed to create user');
};
```

## Mutation Patterns

- Use mutation factories from `@/modules/common` when possible
- ALWAYS invalidate relevant query keys on success
- ALWAYS show toast notifications
- Use `getErrorMessage` for error handling

```typescript
export const useCreateUser = () => {
  const queryClient = useQueryClient();

  return useMutation({
    mutationFn: (data: CreateUserRequest) => usersAPI.createUser(data),
    onSuccess: () => {
      toast.success('User created successfully');
      queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: userQueryKeys.lists() });
    },
    onError: (error: unknown) => {
      toast.error(getErrorMessage(error, 'Failed to create user'));
    },
  });
};
```

## Route Configuration

- Routes are defined in `src/routes/index.tsx` using `createBrowserRouter`
- Use route guards appropriately:
  - `AuthGuard` - for protected routes
  - `GuestGuard` - for auth pages
  - `EmailVerifiedGuard` - for verified-only content
  - `RoleGuard` - for role-based access

```typescript
{
  path: "users",
  element: (
    <RoleGuard minimumRole={Role.Admin} pageLevel>
      <UsersPage />
    </RoleGuard>
  ),
}
```

## Role-based Access Control

- ALWAYS use `Role` enum, never hardcode strings
- Use `useRole` hook for permission checks
- Use `ROLE_LABELS` and `ROLE_BADGE_COLORS` for UI

```typescript
// ✅ Correct
import { Role, useRole, ROLE_LABELS, ROLE_BADGE_COLORS } from "@/modules/auth";
const { isAtLeast } = useRole();
if (isAtLeast(Role.Admin)) { ... }

// ❌ Wrong
if (user.role === "admin") { ... }
```

## Validation

- Validators use Zod and are in `src/libs/validators/`
- Use React Hook Form with `zodResolver`
- Export both validator and inferred type

```typescript
export const createPostValidator = z.object({
  title: z.string().min(1, 'Title is required'),
  content: z.string().min(1, 'Content is required'),
});

export type CreatePostFormData = z.infer<typeof createPostValidator>;
```

## React Hook Form

- Use RHF-adapted components from `@/components/base/_rhf/`
- Available: `RHFInput`, `RHFPasswordInput`, `RHFTextarea`, `RHFCheckbox`
- Always use `zodResolver` with Zod schemas

## Error Boundaries

- ALWAYS wrap data-fetching components with `QueryErrorBoundary`
- Use `ErrorBoundary` for general React errors

```typescript
<QueryErrorBoundary>
  <UsersTable />
</QueryErrorBoundary>
```

## Page Metadata

- ALWAYS set page title using `usePageMetadata` hook
- Include description when appropriate

```typescript
export const UsersPage = () => {
  usePageMetadata({
    title: 'Users',
    description: 'Manage system users', // optional
  });
  // ...
};
```

## File Organization

- Keep files within module structure
- NEVER create helper files outside modules
- Use barrel exports (`index.ts`) for clean imports

```typescript
// ✅ Correct
src / modules / users / libs / userHelpers.ts;

// ❌ Wrong
src / helpers / userHelpers.ts;
```

## Code Style

- Prefer editing existing files over creating new ones
- Keep components focused and single-purpose
- Use TypeScript strict mode
- Run `pnpm lint` before committing
- Always use type-safe patterns
- **DO NOT write comments in code** - Code should be self-documenting through clear naming and structure

## Axios Instances

- Use `axiosInstance` (default) for authenticated requests
- Use `authAxiosInstance` for auth endpoints (login, register)
- NEVER create new axios instances

## Environment Variables

- Add to schema in `src/libs/env.ts`
- Add to `.env.example`
- Access via `env.VITE_*` (type-safe, validated)

## Common Utilities

### Pagination

- Use `PaginatedResponse<T>` and `PaginationMeta` from `@/modules/common`

### Filters

- Use `useTableFilters` hook for URL-synced filters
- Extend `BaseTableFilters` for filter types

### Query Keys

- Use `createQueryKeys` factory for consistent patterns

### CRUD API

- Use `createCrudAPI` factory for standard REST endpoints

## DO NOT

1. ❌ Don't use axios directly in components
2. ❌ Don't define query keys inline
3. ❌ Don't create files outside module structure
4. ❌ Don't mix API calls with UI logic
5. ❌ Don't duplicate types
6. ❌ Don't hardcode strings for roles
7. ❌ Don't forget error boundaries for data fetching
8. ❌ Don't skip page metadata
9. ❌ Don't use generic error messages (use `getErrorMessage`)
10. ❌ Don't create new axios instances
11. ❌ Don't write comments in code - Code should be self-documenting

## When Making Changes

1. Check if module generator can be used first
2. Follow existing patterns in similar modules
3. Use factories from `@/modules/common` when applicable
4. Ensure proper TypeScript types
5. Add error handling with `getErrorMessage`
6. Wrap data-fetching components with `QueryErrorBoundary`
7. Set page metadata
8. Follow import order
9. Run `pnpm type-check` before committing
10. Keep components focused and single-purpose
